Retell AI: Setting Agent Name and Company Name
Oct 11, 2026 · @priya
Option 1: Use dynamic variables
Retell recognises {{agent_name}}-style placeholders as dynamic variables, so you keep the prompt as written and give Retell the values before each call.
1.	Paste the full prompt into the agent's prompt box, leaving the {{ }} placeholders as they are.
2.	Open the Test panel, usually at the bottom or right of the agent page. For a web call, look for where dynamic variable values are entered.
3.	Fill in the values from the table below.
4.	Start the web call.
Variable	Value
agent_name	Priya
agent_gender	female
company_name	Home Credit
customer_name	your own name, e.g. Rahul Sharma
language_to_speak	English
additional_context_from_rag	the sample text from test_scenarios.md
current_date	2026-10-11
current_day	Sunday
current_time	3:30 PM
Retell may fill in some time variables automatically, such as {{current_time}}. Its menus and labels change between versions, so if you can't find the variable inputs, use Option 2.
Option 2: Replace the placeholders with fixed text
This is the safest route for the assignment: you only need working calls and a clean transcript.
1.	Copy system_prompt.md into any text editor.
2.	Use Find and Replace on each placeholder:
o	{{agent_name}} → Priya
o	{{agent_gender}} → female
o	{{company_name}} → Home Credit
o	{{customer_name}} → your name
o	{{language_to_speak}} → English
o	{{current_date}}, {{current_day}}, {{current_time}} → today's values
o	{{additional_context_from_rag}} → the sample context paragraph
3.	Delete the two lines that mention {{conversation_history}} and {{customer_utterance}}. Retell already sends the conversation to the model, and the agent may read the raw placeholder text aloud if you leave them.
4.	Paste the edited prompt into Retell.
Which version to submit
Submit the original prompt with the placeholders, because the assignment says your prompt must account for those variables. Run your test calls with the filled-in version from Option 1 or Option 2.
Greeting line
Retell has a separate Begin Message field, which is the first thing the agent says. If you want the agent to speak first, put this there:
Hello, this is {{agent_name}} from {{company_name}}. May I speak with {{customer_name}}?
If you used Option 2, type the real names instead of the placeholders.

